 "voiceover": "[conversational] Stop only searching LinkedIn. Some jobs are sitting on company career pages.\n\nLots of companies hire through Lever, Ashby and Greenhouse. Google can search those directly, so you spot roles before they hit your feed.\n\n[confident] Step 1. In Google, type: site colon jobs dot lever dot co, then your job title in quotes, then remote. Repeat for Ashby and Greenhouse.\n\nStep 2. Click Tools, then Any time, and pick the past day. Now it's only fresh postings.\n\nStep 3. Paste the results into ChatGPT or Claude and say: [playful] \"Here are new job postings. Keep the ones that match my background and summarize each in one line.\"\n\n[serious] Honest catch: you paste the results yourself, and always check the posting's still open. Do it each morning with your coffee.\n\nWhat job title are you searching for right now?\n\nSend this to the friend who's stuck applying on LinkedIn.",
